Message-ID: <8167262d0904010704v17db3f86n5e8ceba0f4bd40f7@mail.gmail.com>

Xiulian,

If I understand the problem, you have a continuous dependent variable
that is truncated on the left at zero.  Why not use a tobit model?
This is a normal regression truncated at zero from the left.  It's not
a zero-inflated model, but it fits the shape of your data -- and is in
Zelig.

Yours,
Olivia

