Dear professor Lau, 

Thanks a lot for the instruction. I will try the tobit model.
 
But I still have a few concerns: 
1. What do you mean by "normal regression'? You mean normal distribution of the dependent variable? My dependent variable is highly skewed, and even the transformation will not get rid of the skewness because of too many zeros in the data. (That is why I attempted to use a gamma distribution model at the beginning)

2. Can tobit model deals with multilevel issue? (I quickly checked the manual, and it looks like can, but I am not so sure). My data has two levels, city and country--cities are located in countries. At the same time, observations of city and country are repeatedly measured across time. So the data combined both a hierarchical structure and repeated measures. Can tobit model handle that? Please advice. 

3. Can the tobit model do some weighting? My data is extremely unbalanced--some rich country like USA has thousands of cities included in the sample, but for a poor or small country, there is only one or two cities included in the sample. I think I need to weight the data in some way. 

I hope you can give me some advice(I have been struggling with these complicated model issues), and really appreciate your help!

Xiulian 

Ps, 

I also appreciate any advice and help from the rest of the group!





